WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:18.381
Patrasche stopped at the gates of the cathedral.

2
00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:24.875
He had waited here many times while Nello gazed at the beautiful paintings inside.

3
00:00:24.876 --> 00:00:29.821
The tall gates had been blown open by the wind.

4
00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:35.039
Patrasche crept through the gates and up to the cathedral doors.

5
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:41.165
It was long after midnight, and the huge wooden doors were closed.

6
00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:48.359
The Christmas Eve worshippers who had gone to midnight mass had gone home.

7
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.169
Patrasche tried to push open one of the tall doors.

8
00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.501
It was locked.

9
00:00:55.502 --> 00:00:57.943
He tried another one.

10
00:00:57.944 --> 00:01:00.369
It was shut too.

11
00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.050
He walked around the side of the cathedral.

12
00:01:04.051 --> 00:01:11.423
There he found a door someone had forgotten to lock, and he pushed his way inside.

13
00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:14.776
The cathedral was almost empty.

14
00:01:14.777 --> 00:01:21.291
As Patrasche walked along the stone floor, snow fell from his fur.

15
00:01:21.292 --> 00:01:25.193
He left a little trail of snow behind him.

16
00:01:25.194 --> 00:01:29.611
Patrasche saw a figure lying in front of the altar.

17
00:01:29.612 --> 00:01:32.197
It was Nello.

18
00:01:32.198 --> 00:01:37.420
Patrasche crept up and put his paw on Nello's head.

19
00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:43.012
Nello cried out softly and grabbed Patrasche gently.

20
00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:47.808
"Let us lie down and die together," he murmured.

21
00:01:47.809 --> 00:01:52.749
"No one needs us, and we are all alone."

22
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.423
Patrasche put his head upon the young boy's chest.

23
00:01:57.424 --> 00:02:02.353
There were great tears in the dog's sad brown eyes.

24
00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:07.694
The two friends lay close together in the freezing air.

25
00:02:07.695 --> 00:02:12.939
The cathedral's stone floor was as cold as snow.

26
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:17.375
They fell asleep, and together they dreamed.

27
00:02:17.376 --> 00:02:30.020
They dreamed of happier days─when they chased each other through the fields, played with little Alois, or watched boats sail on the canal.

28
00:02:30.021 --> 00:02:35.915
Suddenly, pale rays of white light broke through the darkness.

29
00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:38.511
It was the moon.

30
00:02:38.512 --> 00:02:43.674
The snow had stopped falling and the clouds had slipped away.

31
00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:51.973
The moon's light shone through the high windows in the cathedral's arches.

32
00:02:51.974 --> 00:02:58.197
Rubens' great paintings looked down on the still bodies on the stone floor.

33
00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:03.944
Curtains usually covered the two pictures on either side of the altar.

34
00:03:03.945 --> 00:03:10.428
When Nello had first entered in the dark, he had pulled the curtains aside.

35
00:03:10.429 --> 00:03:17.972
The two paintings were Rubens' The Elevation of the Cross and The Descent from the Cross.

36
00:03:17.973 --> 00:03:22.520
For one moment, they were both visible in the moonlight.

37
00:03:22.521 --> 00:03:25.081
Nello stood up.

38
00:03:25.082 --> 00:03:29.888
He stared at the paintings with joy and awe.

39
00:03:29.889 --> 00:03:32.938
Tears fell from his eyes.

40
00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:36.738
He cried out, "I have seen them at last!

41
00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:38.739
It is enough!"

42
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:43.938
He fell back down and pulled himself close to Patrasche.

43
00:03:43.939 --> 00:03:47.218
They lay together again.

44
00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:52.766
The next morning, they were dead.

45
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:57.961
In the morning, a crowd gathered around their still forms.

46
00:03:57.962 --> 00:04:00.452
The miller was there.

47
00:04:00.453 --> 00:04:05.554
"I was cruel to him," he wept.

48
00:04:05.555 --> 00:04:10.556
"He should have been my son."

49
00:04:10.557 --> 00:04:13.968
Little Alois sobbed bitterly.

50
00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:17.093
She stroked Nello's forehead.

51
00:04:17.094 --> 00:04:21.967
"Today was our playday," she said sadly.

52
00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:25.543
A stranger arrived at the cathedral.

53
00:04:25.544 --> 00:04:31.130
"I am looking for the boy who did this drawing!" he said.

54
00:04:31.131 --> 00:04:36.642
He was a famous artist, and he held Nello's picture in his hand.

55
00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:44.811
"This should be the winning picture," he insisted, "and I want to teach this young man."

56
00:04:44.811 --> 00:04:47.613
But it was too late.

57
00:04:47.614 --> 00:04:54.183
Nello and Patrasche, who had spent their lives together, had died together.

58
00:04:54.184 --> 00:05:01.844
Nello's arms hugged Patrasche's body tightly, so the villagers buried them together too.

59
00:05:01.845 --> 00:05:11.017
The little boy and the dog of Flanders, loyal and loving to the end!
